# SPA fallback — the whole reason a refresh on /login works.
#
# Brevé is one HTML file with a client-side router. Netlify only knows about
# /index.html, so a hard refresh on /login or /signup would otherwise be a
# genuine 404: there is no /login file on disk to serve.
#
# Netlify checks for a matching static file BEFORE applying this rule, so real
# assets (/assets/*, /favicon.svg) are still served normally and only unmatched
# paths fall through to the app. Status 200 rewrites rather than redirects, so
# the URL in the address bar stays /login for React Router to read.
#
# This lives in public/ rather than netlify.toml on purpose: everything in
# public/ is copied into dist/, so the rule travels with the build and applies
# whether you deploy from Git or drag the dist folder onto Netlify.

# Client-side routes that have no matching file on disk — listed explicitly,
# and before the short-link proxy below, so a short code that happens to
# collide with one of these (e.g. someone's code is literally "login") can
# never shadow the real app route.
/login               /index.html   200
/signup              /index.html   200
/forgot-password     /index.html   200
/reset-password/*    /index.html   200
/dashboard           /index.html   200
/dashboard/*         /index.html   200
/pages               /index.html   200
/pages/*             /index.html   200

# Short links & bio pages: bre.ve/<code> is owned entirely by the Express
# server — it renders the redirect itself (plus the expired/passphrase/404
# pages, the passphrase-unlock endpoint, and bio-page open-link tracking),
# no React involved. Proxying (200, not a 3xx redirect) here means the
# address people actually see and share is this frontend's own domain —
# which stays up even when the Render free-tier backend is asleep or
# between deploys — while the real lookup/click-tracking/expiry logic still
# runs on the backend. Netlify makes this request itself, so there's no
# CORS involved. Keep this in sync with SHORT_DOMAIN on the server.
/:code/*   https://breve-server.onrender.com/:code/:splat   200
/:code     https://breve-server.onrender.com/:code          200

/*    /index.html   200
